de missing) at the back.  The waistbands, legs, pockets and fall front are lined with bleached linen.   Two self-covered buttons fasten the fall front.  There are 5 worked buttonholes and 4 embroidered buttons on the outside of each leg above the knee.  The knee bands are embroidered with white, pink and green silk floss. \n\nThe ensemble was altered in the 19th century, probably for theatre costume.  The pleats of the coat were rearranged and the fronts and back relined.  The waistcoat fronts were relined and the centre-back seam unpicked, the edges hemmed and 14 eyelets stitched on the right side of the back and 15 on the left side.  The four buttons fastening the breeches front waistbands were replaced and buttons added to the top of the front waistbands and buttonholes at the back waistband, probably for suspenders/braces."@en , "Man's court coat, waistcoat and breeches, 1788-93, English or French;purple silk velvet/ivory figures silk, embroidered, altered 1870-85"@en ;
